\relax{DEF:FTLE}
        Let $\varphi^t_\omega(x,y)$ be a trajectory of \eqref{eq:ArnoldBruselator}, and let
        $\Phi_t$ be the solution of \eqref{eq: variational_matricial} at time $t$, with initial condition $\Phi_0=\operatorname{id}$. The (maximal) finite-time Lyapunov exponent (FTLE) of \eqref{eq:ArnoldBruselator} for $(\omega,x,y)$ at time $T>0$ is given by 
        \begin{equation}
            \relax{eq:FTLE}
                \lambda^T(\omega,x,y):=\frac{1}{T}\ln\left\Vert \Phi_T\right\Vert,
        \end{equation}
    where $\Vert\cdot\Vert$ is the operator norm or, equivalently, its largest singular value.
